# 4. Buttons in the slide

<div class="code-path">Code: <code>examples/c3-cgp-waving-surface/</code></div>

The objective of this example is to drive the program from buttons written in the text of the slide, outside
the frame of the demo. This way, you can change the model while you speak, the audience sees which state is
shown, and the slide can display a value of the program.

The scene is a grid of 120 x 120 vertices whose positions are updated at each frame: either a ripple from the
center, or parallel waves.

