## Buttons in the slide

The buttons are written in HTML only, and handled by the script `slide-controls.js`. A button of the slide
looks like the following line:

```html
<button data-demo="#surface" data-demo-set="shape=waves">Waves</button>
```

- **data-demo-set** gives the settings to apply when the button is clicked (several settings are separated by `&`, written `&amp;amp;` in HTML).
- **data-demo-value** displays a value of the program, updated live:
  `<span data-demo="#surface" data-demo-value="ampl"></span>`.
- A button gets the class `on` while its settings are the current values of the demo: the audience sees
  which state is displayed.
- **data-demo="#surface"** names the frame driven by the button.
  - *Rem. In reveal.js, all the slides are in the same page: with several demos, give an `id` to each frame,
    and name it on its buttons.*

## The CGP scene

Compared to [example 3](../04_cgp/index.html), the example now has a scene of its own: three files replace
those of the template.

- `main.cpp` only changes by one line: `slide::parse(argc, argv)`.
- The parameters of the wave are declared in `scene.cpp`, as in [example 2](../03_panel/index.html).
- The ImGui window of the template is hidden in a slide (the page already has its panel), unless the address
  contains `?gui=1`.

<div class="callout warn"><div class="callout-title">Note: the wireframe on the web</div>

The function `draw_wireframe()` of CGP uses `glPolygonMode`, which does not exist in WebGL: on the web it draws
nothing, without any error message. In this example, the wireframe is therefore a `curve_drawable` made of
segments (`GL_LINES`), drawn in the same way on the desktop and on the web.

*(This problem was detected by the browser test of the example: the image did not change when the wireframe
was activated.)*

</div>

## The files

```
examples/c3-cgp-waving-surface/
  src/main.cpp       the main() of the template, plus slide::parse
  src/scene.hpp      the parameters of the wave
  src/scene.cpp      the scene: the grid, the wave, the wireframe, the declared parameters
  slides.html        the slide, with its buttons
  demo.json          the browser test of the example
```

